      "content": "To minimize sensor picking up micro-movements and heart rate variability, you can try adjusting your sitting position. Sit with your feet flat on the floor or on a footrest, and keep your knees at or below hip level. This can help reduce peripheral movement and stabilize your heart rate. Additionally, wearing loose, dry clothing and avoiding tight clothing or accessories around your wrists, neck, or waist may also help reduce sensor sensitivity.",
